# --- workerbees: credential blocking ---
# The Python template above covers .env but not the broader key/secret
# patterns. This project's whole premise is that keys live in files and
# never reach a repo, a log, or a model prompt — so block them by shape.
*key*
# Public fixture with no secret
!tests/fixtures/012/openrouter_key_limits.json
# source modules, not credentials (CI import errors otherwise)
!workerbees/keys.py
!agents_inc/keys.py
!tests/test_keys.py
!*.pub
*secret*
*token*
*credential*
*.pem
*.p12
.DS_Store

# workerbees per-workspace state
.workerbees/
.scratch/

# Session handoffs stay local (operator rule 2026-10-01; global ~/.gitignore also covers it)
.claude/handoffs/
# Session handoffs and learning notes stay local (2026-10-01)
docs/HANDOFF.md
docs/governance/ORCHESTRATION-HANDOFF.md
docs/teach-me/

# Operator-only rules (spec 035)
AGENTS.local.md
